course: dictionary
lesson: 11940
title: Cant: a spelling trap and a rare word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words look the same but mean different things, and cant is a trap. In fast texts people write «i cant come today» when they mean «I can't come today». They leave out the apostrophe. A good check is to put cannot into the sentence: if it fits, the word is can't.
explain: The real word cant is rare and formal. As a noun it can mean insincere talk about morals or religion, talk that sounds good but is not honest. «The speaker's words were full of cant» means they sounded kind but were not sincere. As a verb or noun it can also mean a slope or tilt, as in «the shelf had a cant».
explain: Long ago, groups such as thieves used cant for their own special words, called jargon. You will mostly meet this in old books or dictionaries. When you see cant, read the words around it and ask: is it a missing apostrophe, a tilt, or fake talk?
fact: Cant without an apostrophe is often a misspelling of can't, which means cannot.
fact: «I cant swim yet» should be written «I can't swim yet».
fact: As a noun, cant can mean insincere talk about morals or religion.
fact: As a verb or noun, cant can mean a slope or tilt, such as «the shelf had a cant».
fact: Long ago, cant was also the special word list used by groups such as thieves; this is called jargon.
exercise: «We cant go to the park because it is raining.» Which word should replace cant? | can | *can't | could | cants
exercise: «The speech was full of cant, and nobody believed a word of it.» What does cant mean here? | a special word used by a band of friends | a slope on a road | *insincere talk that sounds good but is not honest | a loud, happy song
exercise: «The shelf had a cant, so the cups kept sliding off.» What does cant mean here? | a kind of cake | *a slope or tilt | cannot | a sweet smell
test: Which sentence uses cant to mean a slope? | I cant hear the music from here | The speech was all cant, with no truth in it | The cant of the old preacher made people angry | *The shelf had a cant, so the cups kept sliding
test: Which is the correct way to write the text message «i cant come»? | I could come | I cant come | I cannot cant come | *I can't come
exam: Ella reads a text saying «i cant come» and thinks it means can't. Is she right, and how can she check? | No, it always means a slope, so the text is about a shelf | No, it must be jargon because the apostrophe is missing | Yes, but only because thieves used it that way long ago | *Yes, most texts mean can't, and she can check by putting cannot into the sentence
